{
 "header": {
  "schema": "tick-store-fuzz-1",
  "gate": "G-3",
  "commit": "ea1dde4c02e48961e1369b51183a5c6c6a16e396",
  "statement": "Each libFuzzer target of fuzz/CMakeLists.txt, run for at least 1800 s under the heavy-job lock, with scripts/check.sh's flags and caps, on the existing corpus and the seeds the real encoders write; on Linux, each target whose decode reaches the AVX2 kernels or that verifies CRC32C, which runs the SSE4.2 kernel there, with the level set to avx2. Coverage, corpus and exec/s are libFuzzer's own final figures.",
  "required_seconds": 1800,
  "targets_file": "fuzz/CMakeLists.txt",
  "targets": [
   "fuzz_columns",
   "fuzz_container",
   "fuzz_dictionary",
   "fuzz_gorilla_timestamps",
   "fuzz_gorilla_xor",
   "fuzz_itch_frame",
   "fuzz_itch_message",
   "fuzz_itch_query",
   "fuzz_itch_store",
   "fuzz_pfor",
   "fuzz_run_length",
   "fuzz_stream_vbyte",
   "fuzz_stub_store"
  ],
  "avx2_path_targets": [
   "fuzz_dictionary",
   "fuzz_itch_query",
   "fuzz_itch_store",
   "fuzz_pfor",
   "fuzz_run_length",
   "fuzz_stream_vbyte"
  ],
  "crc32c_path_targets": [
   "fuzz_container",
   "fuzz_itch_query",
   "fuzz_itch_store"
  ],
  "hosts": {
   "macOS": {
    "cpu_model": "Apple M4 Max",
    "kernel": "Darwin 27.2.0",
    "compiler": "clang version 23.1.4 (https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project 7a941dfb2877a0b8cf30323fefa85ad019e0b0f5)",
    "compile_flags": "fuzz preset, RelWithDebInfo: -O2 -g -DNDEBUG -std=c++23 -fsanitize=fuzzer-no-link,address,undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all -fno-omit-frame-pointer, -DTICK_STORE_SIMD_NEON -DTICK_STORE_CRC32C_ARMV8; targets linked with -fsanitize=fuzzer,address,undefined -fuse-ld=lld",
    "sanitizer_options": "ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=1:leak_check_at_exit=0:abort_on_error=0:exitcode=77 UBSAN_OPTIONS=print_stacktrace=1. check.sh's own options plus leak detection, which ASan leaves off on macOS: libFuzzer checks each input for a leak; the check at exit is off because it reports libFuzzer's own RSS thread, never freed",
    "concurrency": "four targets at once, unpinned, in four batches, each batch its own heavy.sh job; the Mac has 16 cores and other sessions' jobs ran beside it",
    "peak_memory": "libFuzzer's peak_rss_mb, and BSD time -l per fuzzer: maximum resident set size and peak memory footprint"
   },
   "Linux": {
    "cpu_model": "AMD Ryzen Embedded V1605B with Radeon Vega Gfx",
    "kernel": "Linux 6.12.116+deb13-amd64",
    "compiler": "clang version 23.1.4 (https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project 7a941dfb2877a0b8cf30323fefa85ad019e0b0f5)",
    "compile_flags": "fuzz preset, RelWithDebInfo: -O2 -g -DNDEBUG -std=c++23 -fsanitize=fuzzer-no-link,address,undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all -fno-omit-frame-pointer, -DTICK_STORE_SIMD_AVX2 -DTICK_STORE_CRC32C_SSE42; targets linked with -fsanitize=fuzzer,address,undefined",
    "sanitizer_options": "ASAN_OPTIONS=abort_on_error=0:exitcode=77 UBSAN_OPTIONS=print_stacktrace=1, as check.sh sets them; LeakSanitizer is on by default on Linux. TICK_STORE_SIMD=avx2, which aborts before the first decode if the build or processor cannot run AVX2. TICK_STORE_CRC32C unset, so store::crc32c() runs the SSE4.2 kernel, which this processor has",
    "concurrency": "three targets at once, each pinned with taskset to one of cpu2, cpu6 and cpu7, in two batches, each its own heavy.sh job; then fuzz_container alone on cpu2, in a third heavy.sh job, for the SSE4.2 CRC32C kernel; cpu4 and cpu5 left alone, no measurement running",
    "peak_memory": "libFuzzer's peak_rss_mb, and the fuzzer's VmHWM read from /proc every 5 s; this host has no GNU time"
   }
  }
 },
